                        "question": "<p><strong><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Read the text and fill in the gaps with the correct form of verbs as per subject and context.</span></strong></p><p><strong><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">It has been over three hundred years since Emperor Shah Jahan of Delhi (a) ____  (build) the Taj Mahal as a tomb for his wife in Agra. Architecturally, it (b) ____  (be) one of the most beautiful buildings in the world. The building (c) ____  (make) of fine white marble with inlays of coloured marblEIt (d) ____  (have) eight sides and many open arches. It (e) ____  (rest) on a platform or terrace of red sandstonEFour slender white towers (f) ____  (rise) from the corners of the terracEA large dome (g) ____  (stand) above the centre of the building. Around this large dome there (h) ____  (be) four smaller domes. Just inside the outer walls, there is an open corridor from which the visitors (i) ____  (look) through carved marble screens into a central room. The bodies of Shah Jahan and his wife Mumtaz (j) ____  (lie) in two graves below this room. </span></strong></p>",
