                        "question": "<p><strong><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Read the text and fill in the gaps with the correct form of verbs as per subject and context.</span></strong></p><p><strong><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Most of the people who (a) ____  (appear) most often and most gloriously in the pages of history (b) ____  (be) great conquerors and generals and soldiers, whereas the people who really (c) ____  (help) civilization forward are often never (d) ____  (mention) at all. We do not know who first (e) ____  (set) a broken leg, or launched a sea worthy boat or (f) ____  (calculate) the length of a year, but we (g) ____  (know) all about the killers and destroyers. People think a great deal of them, so much so that on all the highest pillars in great cities of the world you  (h) ____  (find) figures of a conqueror or a general or a soldier. And I think that most people (i) ____  (believe) that the greatest countries are those that (j) ____  (beat) in the battle the greatest number of countries and ruled over them as conquerors. </span></strong></p>",
