                        "question": "<p><strong><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"> Write a paragraph of about 200 words on \"The Duties and Responsibilities of an Ideal Student\"</span></strong></p>",
                        "explanation": "<p>  <strong>The Qualities and Duties of an Ideal Student/How/ to Become a Good Student/An Ideal Student</strong><br/><br/>An ideal student must possess a certain number of morals and qualities. As a student, the first and foremost duty of an ideal student is to study hard maintaining behavioural code at school. For example, he/she should not idle away his/her time. He/She should be punctual, disciplined and industrious. He/She should avoid bad companies. It is also his/her responsibility to help his/her weaker classmates. The second most important quality of a student is to be social and familial. He/She should be cooperative to his/her family. He/She must engage himself/herself in different kinds of social activities for the betterment of the society as well as the country. Thirdly, an ideal student should be an avid reader. He/She should not confine himself/herself to the prescribed books only; rather he/she should study many other reference books to enrich his/her knowledge. He/She never learns his/her lessons by rote. In addition, an ideal student always takes an active part in other co-curricular activities of the school. These make him/her different from other students. Last but not the least, an ideal student should be polite in his/her behaviour as it highlights his/her other qualities. He/She must obey his/her elders and love the younger ones. To sum up, an ideal student must be an idol to be followed by other students. <strong>    </strong></p>"
